==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Macho Glass Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Macho Crystal Cat''' when obtained from [[Wrath of the Dogelord (Merciless)|Wrath of the Dogelord]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Glass Cat is basically a lighter and single-use version of [[Relentless Gladios (Uber Rare Cat)|Gladios]]; a kamikaze attacker that slows a single traitless enemy for ~8 seconds. Use him against enemies like [[Dober P.D]], [[Kory]] or the [[:Category:Crazed Cat Stages|Crazed]]/[[:Category:Crazed Cat Stages#Manic Cats|Manic]]/[[:Category:Li'l Stages|Li'l Cats]], aside from the [[Crazed Bird Cat (Enemy)|Bird]] [[Manic Flying Cat (Enemy)|Fam]][[Li'l Flying Cat (Enemy)|ily]]. In general, he is good against single traitless bosses, like the [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Heavenly]] [[Mystic Mask Yulala|Tower]] [[Master Uril (Enemy)|bosses]]. Note that [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]] will create [[Wave Attack]]s unless they are knocked back, as Glass Cat's [[Hitbox]] lingers for a brief moment when it attacks.

It is not recommended to upgrade this unit at all until you obtain his true form since the Glass Cat doesn't have noticeable upgrade differences, as due to his metal trait and high speed, he will very likely launch his attack before something like R.Ost can crit on him.

==='''True Form'''===
Macho Crystal Cat improves its stalling capabilities with a guaranteed knockback and longer slow duration. This form has the advantage of interrupting the enemy's attack while also getting them stuck in the back, until the rest of the Cat Army can catch up. The improvements granted by this form are notable in several situations, even against the strongest bosses, but they do not widen this unit's usage, only making him better at what he was already good at. This True Form is a great improvement to a situational cat, and in most cases where you'd use him, like against the [[Heavenly Tower]] bosses.

This form also fixes the problem with wave attackers, as Macho's lingering [[hitbox]] will not trigger the attacks of such units along with their waves. However, be wary when using this form against stages where there is an existence of a backline with Traitless support, unless there are peons within the stage as well which may make Crystal miss.

